From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:57:56 -0400
Subject: tests: BrowserWithTestWindowTest keeps its browser for Stedding's
 unit tests

Chromium 157 removed the browser, its test window and their helpers
(browser(), window(), AddTab(), CreateBrowser(), NavigateAndCommitActiveTab()
and the rest) from BrowserWithTestWindowTest once no upstream test used them
(crrev.com/c/8530766). About thirty of Stedding's unit tests build on them.
This puts them back as they were in 156, with the test window's header the
fixture used to include.

Why: Stedding's unit tests for Spaces, pins, folders, the archive, the
command bar and the sidebar run against a real browser and window.
Removable when: those tests create their own browser and window.
---
 .../base/browser_with_test_window_test.cc     | 95 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../test/base/browser_with_test_window_test.h | 56 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

